{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MNobKZM6DQzZ9HBkgyxPXF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Soften primary contribution framing: QE becomes ''systematic\n2\t  evaluation confirming and extending known UQ principles to structured IE'' (not\n3\t  ''first framework''). Diagnostic contribution needs hedging — ''we identify contributing\n4\t  factors'' rather than ''we diagnose the complete causal chain.'' Drop ''capability-degeneracy\n5\t  tradeoff'' as a named contribution; keep as observed correlation in Discussion.\n6\t  Add paragraph explicitly positioning vs CoCoA/Vashurin 2025 to preempt ''incremental\n7\t  over existing UQ'' criticism. If verifier weak, frame as ''preliminary evidence\n8\t  that supervised approaches are needed'' with Future Work expansion. May need to\n9\t  accept Findings if one reviewer scores ≤3.0.'\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: ner_llama_conll\n12\t  plan_id: exp-017\n13\t  description: LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003, N=8 inference. Cross-model validation\n14\t    for model-agnostic QE claims.\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    greedy_f1: 0.921\n17\t    oracle_f1: 0.944\n18\t    oracle_headroom_pp: 2.3\n19\t    SJ_rho_full: 0.418\n20\t    FK_rho_full: 0.405\n21\t    LP_rho_full: 0.298\n22\t    EM_rho_full: 0.421\n23\t    voting_conf_rho_full: 0.413\n24\t    SJ_AUROC: 0.694\n25\t    EM_AUROC: 0.701\n26\t    LP_AUROC: 0.752\n27\t    selection_SJ_f1: 0.92\n28\t    selection_LP_f1: 0.921\n29\t    selection_vs_greedy_pp: -0.1\n30\t    structural_beats_surface: true\n31\t    degeneracy_rate: 0.55\n32\t  result_rationale: 在 median 档下，LLaMA CoNLL 复现 Qwen CoNLL 的核心模式（structural > surface，selection\n33\t    ≈ greedy），但不会显著超越。CoNLL 高 baseline F1 (>0.91) 导致高 degeneracy (~55%)，oracle headroom\n34\t    仅 2.3pp，selection 无法显著超过 greedy。SJ_rho ~0.42 与 Qwen CoNLL (0.436) 一致，验证 cross-model\n35\t    但 reviewer 会指出 '两个 8B 模型不足以证明 model-agnostic'——这正是 A6 PARTIAL 假设的体现。LP AUROC 偏高（0.75）因为\n36\t    CoNLL 高精度实例的 LP 能有效区分 perfect vs near-perfect，但 rho 仍低于 structural signals。\n37\t  tables:\n38\t  - name: 'Table: LLaMA CoNLL-2003 QE Metrics (N=8, T=1.0)'\n39\t    columns:\n40\t    - Signal\n41\t    - ρ_full\n42\t    - τ_full\n43\t    - AUROC\n44\t    - ECE\n45\t    - Sel_F1\n46\t    rows:\n47\t    - - SJ\n48\t      - 0.418\n49\t      - 0.372\n50\t      - 0.694\n51\t      - 0.112\n52\t      - 0.92\n53\t    - - FK\n54\t      - 0.405\n55\t      - 0.361\n56\t      - 0.688\n57\t      - 0.108\n58\t      - 0.919\n59\t    - - EM\n60\t      - 0.421\n61\t      - 0.377\n62\t      - 0.701\n63\t      - 0.105\n64\t      - 0.919\n65\t    - - Voting_conf\n66\t      - 0.413\n67\t      - 0.368\n68\t      - 0.698\n69\t      - 0.092\n70\t      - 0.92\n71\t    - - Logprob\n72\t      - 0.298\n73\t      - 0.238\n74\t      - 0.752\n75\t      - 0.131\n76\t      - 0.921\n77\t    - - Greedy\n78\t      - —\n79\t      - —\n80\t      - —\n81\t      - —\n82\t      - 0.921\n83\t    - - Oracle\n84\t      - —\n85\t      - —\n86\t      - —\n87\t      - —\n88\t      - 0.944\n89\t  figures_description:\n90\t  - Bar chart comparing SJ_rho across 3 model configs (Qwen-8B, Qwen-4B, LLaMA-8B)\n91\t    on CoNLL — all in 0.40-0.45 range, demonstrating cross-model stability\n92\t  analysis: 'Cross-model validation holds but provides incremental rather than decisive\n93\t    evidence. Reviewer likely notes: (1) both are 8B-class models — no evidence for\n94\t    smaller/larger scales; (2) CoNLL''s high baseline makes selection analysis trivial\n95\t    (headroom <3pp). In median tier, this supports the QE contribution as ''solid\n96\t    engineering'' (A1 PARTIAL) but doesn''t push novelty score above 3-4 because the\n97\t    finding (structural signals generalize across architectures) is expected from\n98\t    UQ literature.'\n99\t- name: simple_verifier_baseline\n100\t  plan_id: exp-019\n101\t  description: Logistic regression on 5 QE signals as supervised verifier. Tests whether\n102\t    oracle gap is closable with supervision. Training on SciERC NER+RE with F1 labels.\n103\t  expected_results:\n104\t    ner_verifier_selection_f1: 0.655\n105\t    ner_greedy_f1: 0.644\n106\t    ner_oracle_f1: 0.776\n107\t    ner_gap_closure_pct: 8.3\n108\t    ner_verifier_vs_greedy_pp: 1.1\n109\t    re_verifier_selection_f1: 0.412\n110\t    re_greedy_f1: 0.404\n111\t    re_oracle_f1: 0.585\n112\t    re_gap_closure_pct: 4.4\n113\t    re_verifier_vs_greedy_pp: 0.8\n114\t    cv_auroc_ner: 0.772\n115\t    cv_auroc_re: 0.718\n116\t    feature_importance_top: EM > voting_conf > SJ > LP > FK\n117\t    overfitting_risk: moderate (n=529 NER, n=397 RE, 5-fold CV)\n118\t    training_time_minutes: 12\n119\t  result_rationale: 在 median 档下 (A5 FAILS/WEAK)，trained verifier 完成但 gap closure <15%。逻辑回归在\n120\t    5 个高度相关的信号上（SJ-LP pearson=0.57）受限于 feature redundancy——exp-016 已经显示 ensemble 无优势。NER\n121\t    gap closure ~8% (1.1pp) 因为：(1) 监督信号确实比 unsupervised heuristic 好（能学到非线性组合），但 (2)\n122\t    输入信号本身信息量有限（within-instance discriminative power 低），5-fold CV 在 n=529 上容易 overfit。RE\n123\t    更弱 (4.4%) 因为 binary dominance (43% F1=0) 使得回归主要学到 'zero vs non-zero' 而非 quality\n124\t    gradient。Reviewer 评价：'path forward evidence suggestive not definitive'——8% closure\n125\t    不足以作为独立贡献，但支持 'trained verifiers needed' 的 future work framing。\n126\t  tables:\n127\t  - name: 'Table: Supervised Verifier vs Unsupervised Signals (5-fold CV)'\n128\t    columns:\n129\t    - Method\n130\t    - NER Sel_F1\n131\t    - NER Δ_greedy\n132\t    - NER Gap%\n133\t    - RE Sel_F1\n134\t    - RE Δ_greedy\n135\t    - RE Gap%\n136\t    rows:\n137\t    - - Greedy (T=0)\n138\t      - 0.644\n139\t      - —\n140\t      - —\n141\t      - 0.404\n142\t      - —\n143\t      - —\n144\t    - - Best unsupervised (LP)\n145\t      - 0.65\n146\t      - +0.6pp\n147\t      - 4.5%\n148\t      - 0.409\n149\t      - +0.5pp\n150\t      - 2.8%\n151\t    - - LR verifier (5 signals)\n152\t      - 0.655\n153\t      - +1.1pp\n154\t      - 8.3%\n155\t      - 0.412\n156\t      - +0.8pp\n157\t      - 4.4%\n158\t    - - Oracle\n159\t      - 0.776\n160\t      - +13.2pp\n161\t      - 100%\n162\t      - 0.585\n163\t      - +18.1pp\n164\t      - 100%\n165\t  - name: 'Table: Feature Importance (Logistic Regression Coefficients, NER)'\n166\t    columns:\n167\t    - Signal\n168\t    - Mean Coeff\n169\t    - Std across folds\n170\t    rows:\n171\t    - - EM\n172\t      - 0.42\n173\t      - 0.08\n174\t    - - voting_conf\n175\t      - 0.31\n176\t      - 0.06\n177\t    - - SJ\n178\t      - 0.22\n179\t      - 0.09\n180\t    - - logprob\n181\t      - 0.18\n182\t      - 0.11\n183\t    - - FK\n184\t      - 0.07\n185\t      - 0.05\n186\t  figures_description:\n187\t  - 'Selection curve (F1 vs method) showing: random < unsupervised cluster (LP/SJ/VC\n188\t    all within 0.5pp) < LR verifier (+1.1pp) << oracle (+13.2pp). The massive remaining\n189\t    gap visualizes why ''trained verifier needed'' is understatement.'\n190\t  analysis: 'Verifier closes 8.3% of NER gap — statistically significant (paired t-test\n191\t    p<0.05 across folds) but practically marginal. This is precisely the A5 WEAK outcome:\n192\t    enough to say ''supervision helps'' but not enough to constitute a paper contribution.\n193\t    One reviewer will say ''you showed logistic regression on your own features slightly\n194\t    beats your own features used individually — this is expected and not interesting.''\n195\t    Counter-argument: the 92% gap that remains proves the signals are fundamentally\n196\t    limited, not just suboptimally combined. Paper frames as: ''preliminary supervised\n197\t    baseline confirms gap is partially closable, motivating dedicated learned verifiers\n198\t    as future work.'' Findings-level contribution at best for this component.'\n199\t- name: claim_audit\n200\t  plan_id: exp-024\n201\t  description: Systematic numerical consistency audit across all paper sections. Resolve\n202\t    contradictions between Discussion, Limitations, Abstract, and source experiment\n203\t    data.\n204\t  expected_results:\n205\t    contradictions_found: 4\n206\t    critical_contradictions: 1\n207\t    minor_inconsistencies: 3\n208\t    sections_affected:\n209\t    - Discussion\n210\t    - Limitations\n211\t    - Abstract\n212\t    - Introduction\n213\t    resolution_time_hours: 3\n214\t    key_contradiction_1: Discussion '+0.1pp over single-sample' vs Limitations '+0.4pp\n215\t      over greedy' — source truth is +0.6pp (logprob NER, exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap)\n216\t    key_contradiction_2: Abstract AUROC '0.82' refers to CoNLL EM (0.816) but body\n217\t      text reports SciERC EM (0.749) — need to clarify which dataset/metric the abstract\n218\t      claim uses\n219\t    key_contradiction_3: 'Introduction claims ''5 confidence signals across 4 families''\n220\t      but method section describes 5 signals in 3 families (structural: SJ/FK/EM;\n221\t      voting: VC; probabilistic: LP)'\n222\t    key_contradiction_4: 'Capability-degeneracy numbers: Discussion says ''CoNLL 58%''\n223\t      but exp_012_rerun_1024 shows tied_fraction=0.597 for constrained, referencing\n224\t      different definitions of degeneracy'\n225\t  result_rationale: 在 median 档下，audit 发现的矛盾是可修复的 housekeeping 问题，不影响核心结论但如果未修会被 reviewer\n226\t    作为 soundness concern 扣分（A3 PARTIAL 中 reviewer 对 single-point ablation 的质疑部分源于数字不一致降低可信度）。最关键矛盾是\n227\t    AUROC 0.82 的来源——paper_framing.md 中 Claim 1 说 'AUROC up to 0.82' 但实际最高是 CoNLL EM_AUROC=0.816\n228\t    (exp_002) 或 CoNLL N=16 EM_AUROC=0.841 (exp_002_conll_n16)。Median tier soundness\n229\t    score 3.5-4.5 意味着这些矛盾被发现但不致命——修复后不影响结论但审稿时若未修会被扣 0.5 分。\n230\t  tables:\n231\t  - name: 'Table: Claim Audit Results'\n232\t    columns:\n233\t    - Location\n234\t    - Claimed Value\n235\t    - Source Truth\n236\t    - Resolution\n237\t    rows:\n238\t    - - 'Abstract: ''AUROC up to 0.82'''\n239\t      - '0.82'\n240\t      - CoNLL EM 0.816 (N=8) or 0.841 (N=16)\n241\t      - Use 0.82 rounded from 0.816, cite N=8 CoNLL\n242\t    - - 'Discussion: ''+0.1pp'''\n243\t      - +0.1pp over single-sample\n244\t      - +0.6pp LP vs greedy (NER, p=0.39 n.s.)\n245\t      - Correct to '+0.6pp (n.s., p=0.39)'\n246\t    - - 'Limitations: ''+0.4pp'''\n247\t      - +0.4pp over greedy\n248\t      - Same metric different rounding\n249\t      - Unify to +0.6pp with CI\n250\t    - - 'Intro: ''4 families'''\n251\t      - 4 signal families\n252\t      - 3 families (structural/voting/probabilistic)\n253\t      - Correct to '3 families' or redefine EM as separate family\n254\t  figures_description: []\n255\t  analysis: Audit 是纯 hygiene 任务但在 median 档下至关重要——soundness score 3.5-4.5 的差异往往取决于\n256\t    reviewer 是否信任作者的细节把控。AUROC 0.82 引用的歧义（CoNLL vs SciERC, N=8 vs N=16）如果 reviewer\n257\t    自己算对不上会直接降 soundness 0.5 分。修复耗时 ~3h，全部是文本编辑，零实验成本。在 median tier 下这些修复是 necessary\n258\t    condition for 3.5 soundness——如果不修，可能跌到 3.0 (Findings boundary)。\n259\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d14e849-04d8-4a95-8f72-941f894ab1f4","uuid":"a1975636-fe64-4d39-b8c6-0de06d0bd6e9","timestamp":"2026-05-16T12:02:16.643Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T113255/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Soften primary contribution framing: QE becomes ''systematic\n  evaluation confirming and extending known UQ principles to structured IE'' (not\n  ''first framework''). Diagnostic contribution needs hedging — ''we identify contributing\n  factors'' rather than ''we diagnose the complete causal chain.'' Drop ''capability-degeneracy\n  tradeoff'' as a named contribution; keep as observed correlation in Discussion.\n  Add paragraph explicitly positioning vs CoCoA/Vashurin 2025 to preempt ''incremental\n  over existing UQ'' criticism. If verifier weak, frame as ''preliminary evidence\n  that supervised approaches are needed'' with Future Work expansion. May need to\n  accept Findings if one reviewer scores ≤3.0.'\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: ner_llama_conll\n  plan_id: exp-017\n  description: LLaMA-3.1-8B fine-tuned on CoNLL-2003, N=8 inference. Cross-model validation\n    for model-agnostic QE claims.\n  expected_results:\n    greedy_f1: 0.921\n    oracle_f1: 0.944\n    oracle_headroom_pp: 2.3\n    SJ_rho_full: 0.418\n    FK_rho_full: 0.405\n    LP_rho_full: 0.298\n    EM_rho_full: 0.421\n    voting_conf_rho_full: 0.413\n    SJ_AUROC: 0.694\n    EM_AUROC: 0.701\n    LP_AUROC: 0.752\n    selection_SJ_f1: 0.92\n    selection_LP_f1: 0.921\n    selection_vs_greedy_pp: -0.1\n    structural_beats_surface: true\n    degeneracy_rate: 0.55\n  result_rationale: 在 median 档下，LLaMA CoNLL 复现 Qwen CoNLL 的核心模式（structural > surface，selection\n    ≈ greedy），但不会显著超越。CoNLL 高 baseline F1 (>0.91) 导致高 degeneracy (~55%)，oracle headroom\n    仅 2.3pp，selection 无法显著超过 greedy。SJ_rho ~0.42 与 Qwen CoNLL (0.436) 一致，验证 cross-model\n    但 reviewer 会指出 '两个 8B 模型不足以证明 model-agnostic'——这正是 A6 PARTIAL 假设的体现。LP AUROC 偏高（0.75）因为\n    CoNLL 高精度实例的 LP 能有效区分 perfect vs near-perfect，但 rho 仍低于 structural signals。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: LLaMA CoNLL-2003 QE Metrics (N=8, T=1.0)'\n    columns:\n    - Signal\n    - ρ_full\n    - τ_full\n    - AUROC\n    - ECE\n    - Sel_F1\n    rows:\n    - - SJ\n      - 0.418\n      - 0.372\n      - 0.694\n      - 0.112\n      - 0.92\n    - - FK\n      - 0.405\n      - 0.361\n      - 0.688\n      - 0.108\n      - 0.919\n    - - EM\n      - 0.421\n      - 0.377\n      - 0.701\n      - 0.105\n      - 0.919\n    - - Voting_conf\n      - 0.413\n      - 0.368\n      - 0.698\n      - 0.092\n      - 0.92\n    - - Logprob\n      - 0.298\n      - 0.238\n      - 0.752\n      - 0.131\n      - 0.921\n    - - Greedy\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 0.921\n    - - Oracle\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 0.944\n  figures_description:\n  - Bar chart comparing SJ_rho across 3 model configs (Qwen-8B, Qwen-4B, LLaMA-8B)\n    on CoNLL — all in 0.40-0.45 range, demonstrating cross-model stability\n  analysis: 'Cross-model validation holds but provides incremental rather than decisive\n    evidence. Reviewer likely notes: (1) both are 8B-class models — no evidence for\n    smaller/larger scales; (2) CoNLL''s high baseline makes selection analysis trivial\n    (headroom <3pp). In median tier, this supports the QE contribution as ''solid\n    engineering'' (A1 PARTIAL) but doesn''t push novelty score above 3-4 because the\n    finding (structural signals generalize across architectures) is expected from\n    UQ literature.'\n- name: simple_verifier_baseline\n  plan_id: exp-019\n  description: Logistic regression on 5 QE signals as supervised verifier. Tests whether\n    oracle gap is closable with supervision. Training on SciERC NER+RE with F1 labels.\n  expected_results:\n    ner_verifier_selection_f1: 0.655\n    ner_greedy_f1: 0.644\n    ner_oracle_f1: 0.776\n    ner_gap_closure_pct: 8.3\n    ner_verifier_vs_greedy_pp: 1.1\n    re_verifier_selection_f1: 0.412\n    re_greedy_f1: 0.404\n    re_oracle_f1: 0.585\n    re_gap_closure_pct: 4.4\n    re_verifier_vs_greedy_pp: 0.8\n    cv_auroc_ner: 0.772\n    cv_auroc_re: 0.718\n    feature_importance_top: EM > voting_conf > SJ > LP > FK\n    overfitting_risk: moderate (n=529 NER, n=397 RE, 5-fold CV)\n    training_time_minutes: 12\n  result_rationale: 在 median 档下 (A5 FAILS/WEAK)，trained verifier 完成但 gap closure <15%。逻辑回归在\n    5 个高度相关的信号上（SJ-LP pearson=0.57）受限于 feature redundancy——exp-016 已经显示 ensemble 无优势。NER\n    gap closure ~8% (1.1pp) 因为：(1) 监督信号确实比 unsupervised heuristic 好（能学到非线性组合），但 (2)\n    输入信号本身信息量有限（within-instance discriminative power 低），5-fold CV 在 n=529 上容易 overfit。RE\n    更弱 (4.4%) 因为 binary dominance (43% F1=0) 使得回归主要学到 'zero vs non-zero' 而非 quality\n    gradient。Reviewer 评价：'path forward evidence suggestive not definitive'——8% closure\n    不足以作为独立贡献，但支持 'trained verifiers needed' 的 future work framing。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Supervised Verifier vs Unsupervised Signals (5-fold CV)'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - NER Sel_F1\n    - NER Δ_greedy\n    - NER Gap%\n    - RE Sel_F1\n    - RE Δ_greedy\n    - RE Gap%\n    rows:\n    - - Greedy (T=0)\n      - 0.644\n      - —\n      - —\n      - 0.404\n      - —\n      - —\n    - - Best unsupervised (LP)\n      - 0.65\n      - +0.6pp\n      - 4.5%\n      - 0.409\n      - +0.5pp\n      - 2.8%\n    - - LR verifier (5 signals)\n      - 0.655\n      - +1.1pp\n      - 8.3%\n      - 0.412\n      - +0.8pp\n      - 4.4%\n    - - Oracle\n      - 0.776\n      - +13.2pp\n      - 100%\n      - 0.585\n      - +18.1pp\n      - 100%\n  - name: 'Table: Feature Importance (Logistic Regression Coefficients, NER)'\n    columns:\n    - Signal\n    - Mean Coeff\n    - Std across folds\n    rows:\n    - - EM\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.08\n    - - voting_conf\n      - 0.31\n      - 0.06\n    - - SJ\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.09\n    - - logprob\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.11\n    - - FK\n      - 0.07\n      - 0.05\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Selection curve (F1 vs method) showing: random < unsupervised cluster (LP/SJ/VC\n    all within 0.5pp) < LR verifier (+1.1pp) << oracle (+13.2pp). The massive remaining\n    gap visualizes why ''trained verifier needed'' is understatement.'\n  analysis: 'Verifier closes 8.3% of NER gap — statistically significant (paired t-test\n    p<0.05 across folds) but practically marginal. This is precisely the A5 WEAK outcome:\n    enough to say ''supervision helps'' but not enough to constitute a paper contribution.\n    One reviewer will say ''you showed logistic regression on your own features slightly\n    beats your own features used individually — this is expected and not interesting.''\n    Counter-argument: the 92% gap that remains proves the signals are fundamentally\n    limited, not just suboptimally combined. Paper frames as: ''preliminary supervised\n    baseline confirms gap is partially closable, motivating dedicated learned verifiers\n    as future work.'' Findings-level contribution at best for this component.'\n- name: claim_audit\n  plan_id: exp-024\n  description: Systematic numerical consistency audit across all paper sections. Resolve\n    contradictions between Discussion, Limitations, Abstract, and source experiment\n    data.\n  expected_results:\n    contradictions_found: 4\n    critical_contradictions: 1\n    minor_inconsistencies: 3\n    sections_affected:\n    - Discussion\n    - Limitations\n    - Abstract\n    - Introduction\n    resolution_time_hours: 3\n    key_contradiction_1: Discussion '+0.1pp over single-sample' vs Limitations '+0.4pp\n      over greedy' — source truth is +0.6pp (logprob NER, exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap)\n    key_contradiction_2: Abstract AUROC '0.82' refers to CoNLL EM (0.816) but body\n      text reports SciERC EM (0.749) — need to clarify which dataset/metric the abstract\n      claim uses\n    key_contradiction_3: 'Introduction claims ''5 confidence signals across 4 families''\n      but method section describes 5 signals in 3 families (structural: SJ/FK/EM;\n      voting: VC; probabilistic: LP)'\n    key_contradiction_4: 'Capability-degeneracy numbers: Discussion says ''CoNLL 58%''\n      but exp_012_rerun_1024 shows tied_fraction=0.597 for constrained, referencing\n      different definitions of degeneracy'\n  result_rationale: 在 median 档下，audit 发现的矛盾是可修复的 housekeeping 问题，不影响核心结论但如果未修会被 reviewer\n    作为 soundness concern 扣分（A3 PARTIAL 中 reviewer 对 single-point ablation 的质疑部分源于数字不一致降低可信度）。最关键矛盾是\n    AUROC 0.82 的来源——paper_framing.md 中 Claim 1 说 'AUROC up to 0.82' 但实际最高是 CoNLL EM_AUROC=0.816\n    (exp_002) 或 CoNLL N=16 EM_AUROC=0.841 (exp_002_conll_n16)。Median tier soundness\n    score 3.5-4.5 意味着这些矛盾被发现但不致命——修复后不影响结论但审稿时若未修会被扣 0.5 分。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Claim Audit Results'\n    columns:\n    - Location\n    - Claimed Value\n    - Source Truth\n    - Resolution\n    rows:\n    - - 'Abstract: ''AUROC up to 0.82'''\n      - '0.82'\n      - CoNLL EM 0.816 (N=8) or 0.841 (N=16)\n      - Use 0.82 rounded from 0.816, cite N=8 CoNLL\n    - - 'Discussion: ''+0.1pp'''\n      - +0.1pp over single-sample\n      - +0.6pp LP vs greedy (NER, p=0.39 n.s.)\n      - Correct to '+0.6pp (n.s., p=0.39)'\n    - - 'Limitations: ''+0.4pp'''\n      - +0.4pp over greedy\n      - Same metric different rounding\n      - Unify to +0.6pp with CI\n    - - 'Intro: ''4 families'''\n      - 4 signal families\n      - 3 families (structural/voting/probabilistic)\n      - Correct to '3 families' or redefine EM as separate family\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Audit 是纯 hygiene 任务但在 median 档下至关重要——soundness score 3.5-4.5 的差异往往取决于\n    reviewer 是否信任作者的细节把控。AUROC 0.82 引用的歧义（CoNLL vs SciERC, N=8 vs N=16）如果 reviewer\n    自己算对不上会直接降 soundness 0.5 分。修复耗时 ~3h，全部是文本编辑，零实验成本。在 median tier 下这些修复是 necessary\n    condition for 3.5 soundness——如果不修，可能跌到 3.0 (Findings boundary)。\n","numLines":259,"startLine":1,"totalLines":259}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CxendupnTLKh1HZ52JbzzQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X\",\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting\"},{\"title\":\"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026's review process, though the specific reviewer guidelines review form details are limited in these results. Here's what I found:\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference.\n\nBoth submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform, where authors submit articles to ARR and receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors.\n\nRegarding review timelines, if you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\nFor specific details about the reviewer guidelines and the actual review form structure, you would likely need to:\n\n1. Visit the official EMNLP 2026 website at https://2026.emnlp.org/\n2. Check the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) guidelines at aclrollingreview.org, as EMNLP 2026 uses ARR for its review process\n3. Access OpenReview directly at openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026 once reviews are open\n\nThe specific review form and detailed guidelines are typically made available when reviewer assignments are sent out and the review process begins.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d14e849-04d8-4a95-8f72-941f894ab1f4","uuid":"34a2133f-2162-439d-9ea3-2976d8047dcd","timestamp":"2026-05-16T12:02:20.698Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VNFnXv2yscMMMZuXW2JBv3","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"EMNLP | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 (@emnlpmeeting) · X","url":"https://twitter.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 (@emnlpmeeting) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/emnlpmeeting"},{"title":"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026's review process, though the specific reviewer guidelines review form details are limited in these results. Here's what I found:\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference.\n\nBoth submissions of articles for review and commitment of reviewed articles to the conference will be performed via the Open Review platform, where authors submit articles to ARR and receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors.\n\nRegarding review timelines, if you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews by July 29.\n\nFor specific details about the reviewer guidelines and the actual review form structure, you would likely need to:\n\n1. Visit the official EMNLP 2026 website at https://2026.emnlp.org/\n2. Check the ACL Rolling Review (ARR) guidelines at aclrollingreview.org, as EMNLP 2026 uses ARR for its review process\n3. Access OpenReview directly at openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026 once reviews are open\n\nThe specific review form and detailed guidelines are typically made available when reviewer assignments are sent out and the review process begins."],"durationSeconds":5.256640606000001}}
