{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GS5rpdqKju7xpy9k1hhGMU","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review 2025 2026 review form scoring rubric dimensions\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/acl-rolling-review\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review scoring rubric for 2025-2026:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe excitement score is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper, capturing more subjective preferences about whether work is interesting.\n\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review, and if you give a low soundness score without finding any major faults, it means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation.\n\nThe review form focuses on these three main dimensions for the 2025-2026 cycles rather than a more detailed rubric with additional scoring dimensions. For more detailed information about the review form itself, you can visit the official ACL Rolling Review review form page at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d14e849-04d8-4a95-8f72-941f894ab1f4","uuid":"64847504-2d14-41bc-b612-981ea6f943ad","timestamp":"2026-05-16T12:02:32.670Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review 2025 2026 review form scoring rubric dimensions","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Em6R2ZcEQSW7qe8ESuGuWZ","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/cfp.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/cfp.md"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ACL ARR | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/acl-rolling-review"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about the ACL Rolling Review scoring rubric for 2025-2026:\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\nThe excitement score is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper, capturing more subjective preferences about whether work is interesting.\n\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review, and if you give a low soundness score without finding any major faults, it means that your review is not a faithful explanation of your recommendation.\n\nThe review form focuses on these three main dimensions for the 2025-2026 cycles rather than a more detailed rubric with additional scoring dimensions. For more detailed information about the review form itself, you can visit the official ACL Rolling Review review form page at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform."],"durationSeconds":5.154812747}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vpbxhx3Luzt7ZKL9wbpVqp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 acceptance rate reviewer scoring scale guidelines\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Decisions: Community Insights and the Controversial Desk Rejections | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/131/emnlp-2025-decisions-community-insights-and-the-controversial-desk-rejections\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\"},{\"title\":\"Conference Decisions · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/proceedings/10.5555/1613715\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"OpenReviewer: A Specialized Large Language Model for Generating Critical Scientific Paper Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.11948v3\"},{\"title\":\"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2025's acceptance rate and reviewer scoring guidelines:\n\n## EMNLP 2025 Acceptance Rate\n\nThe Main acceptance rate for EMNLP 2025 is just over 22%.\n\n## Reviewer Scoring Scale Guidelines\n\nEMNLP 2025 uses a 5-point scale with half-point increments for scoring. The guidelines provide specific instructions for reviewers:\n\n- A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, though reviewers are encouraged to take a stand by selecting 2.5 or 3.5; however, if a paper is deemed borderline or reviewers cannot decide, they should use 3.\n\n- Detailed explanations for each point level are provided in the review form, and these numbers are a concise way of expressing overall opinion and the relative importance of evaluated factors.\n\n## Meta-Review Score Insights\n\nFrom the community analysis of EMNLP 2025 decisions, some patterns emerged regarding how meta-review scores influenced decisions:\n\n- Meta scores ≥ 3.5 often led to Main acceptance, even when individual reviewer scores were mediocre (e.g., 2.67)\n- Meta scores < 3 almost always resulted in rejection, with rare exceptions\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d14e849-04d8-4a95-8f72-941f894ab1f4","uuid":"e87a584f-5919-4916-91a9-bf23644258ab","timestamp":"2026-05-16T12:02:38.235Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 acceptance rate reviewer scoring scale guidelines","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01QYUhX7HhNLNU9c4jwpAjNA","content":[{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Decisions: Community Insights and the Controversial Desk Rejections | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/131/emnlp-2025-decisions-community-insights-and-the-controversial-desk-rejections"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/emnlp-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"},{"title":"Conference Decisions · GitHub","url":"https://gist.github.com/antonisa/2158dee79179c7c49304ef353887bfa0"},{"title":"EMNLP Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/emnlp-statistics/"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/proceedings/10.5555/1613715"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"OpenReviewer: A Specialized Large Language Model for Generating Critical Scientific Paper Reviews","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.11948v3"},{"title":"[EMNLP 2025] First Call for Papers | ACL Member Portal","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/portal/content/emnlp-2025-first-call-papers"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about EMNLP 2025's acceptance rate and reviewer scoring guidelines:\n\n## EMNLP 2025 Acceptance Rate\n\nThe Main acceptance rate for EMNLP 2025 is just over 22%.\n\n## Reviewer Scoring Scale Guidelines\n\nEMNLP 2025 uses a 5-point scale with half-point increments for scoring. The guidelines provide specific instructions for reviewers:\n\n- A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, though reviewers are encouraged to take a stand by selecting 2.5 or 3.5; however, if a paper is deemed borderline or reviewers cannot decide, they should use 3.\n\n- Detailed explanations for each point level are provided in the review form, and these numbers are a concise way of expressing overall opinion and the relative importance of evaluated factors.\n\n## Meta-Review Score Insights\n\nFrom the community analysis of EMNLP 2025 decisions, some patterns emerged regarding how meta-review scores influenced decisions:\n\n- Meta scores ≥ 3.5 often led to Main acceptance, even when individual reviewer scores were mediocre (e.g., 2.67)\n- Meta scores < 3 almost always resulted in rejection, with rare exceptions"],"durationSeconds":10.096158357999997}}
