{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UgJ2tB4GWcupUSPaVYZ3cj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org review form soundness excitement overall scale 1-5\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"}]\n\nI found information about the ACL Rolling Review form. Based on the search results, here's what the review form contains regarding soundness, excitement, and overall assessment:\n\n## Soundness Score\n\nThe form asks: \"Given that this is a short/long paper, is it sufficiently sound and thorough? Does it clearly state scientific claims and provide adequate support for them?\" The scale includes 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n## Excitement Score\n\nThe form asks \"How exciting is this paper for you?\" with the note that \"Excitement is subjective, and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field.\" The scale includes 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend the paper to others and/or attend its presentation) and 4 = Exciting (would mention the paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation).\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The Overall assessment score is \"an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue\" and is \"a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\"\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d14e849-04d8-4a95-8f72-941f894ab1f4","uuid":"8b85a894-08a4-4b5a-839a-d2c89d863bc5","timestamp":"2026-05-16T12:02:48.735Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org review form soundness excitement overall scale 1-5","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CMXnaJNEDArjdRKa9fd1pn","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"}]},"I found information about the ACL Rolling Review form. Based on the search results, here's what the review form contains regarding soundness, excitement, and overall assessment:\n\n## Soundness Score\n\nThe form asks: \"Given that this is a short/long paper, is it sufficiently sound and thorough? Does it clearly state scientific claims and provide adequate support for them?\" The scale includes 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n## Excitement Score\n\nThe form asks \"How exciting is this paper for you?\" with the note that \"Excitement is subjective, and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field.\" The scale includes 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend the paper to others and/or attend its presentation) and 4 = Exciting (would mention the paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation).\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation. The Overall assessment score is \"an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue\" and is \"a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\""],"durationSeconds":6.139285285999998}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CMzJip6QBbEV8JPLnZsj9m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough information about the review form. Let me also fetch the WebFetch tool to get the exact scoring rubric from aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\nActually, I have enough information. Let me summarize what I know:\n\nARR Review Form (used by EMNLP 2026):\n- **Soundness**: 1-5 scale (5=Excellent, 4=Strong, 3=Acceptable, 2=Poor, 1=Major issues)\n- **Excitement**: 1-5 scale (5=Highly Exciting, 4=Exciting, 3=Ambivalent, 2=Below Average, 1=Not Exciting)\n\n\n- **Overall Assessment**: 1-5 scale, composite of soundness, excitement, novelty, impact\n- EMNLP acceptance rate ~22%\n\nNow I'm setting up the full review process with two specialized reviewers—one focusing on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work—and then running them through a structured roundtable discussion with independent reviews, cross-sharing, convergence, and synthesis phases. Let me launch both reviewers as parallel agents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":681,"cache_read_input_tokens":55079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":681},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d14e849-04d8-4a95-8f72-941f894ab1f4","uuid":"bf390dcb-d356-40f7-bf8c-23f35050ac2f"}
