{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01CT51xX871hYcHTp9eMNHW6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AnVE1Ax8wdSzUkQ7MfoAQN","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Roundtable convergence discussion","prompt":"You are the Area Chair moderating a roundtable convergence discussion between two reviewers of an EMNLP 2026 submission.\n\n## Paper\n\"Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors: Why Confidence Signals Cannot Scale Structured Information Extraction\"\n\nEvaluates 5 confidence signals for structured IE (NER/RE). Finds signals predict quality at population level (AUROC~0.82, ρ~0.45) but fail at instance-level selection (+0.6pp over greedy, n.s., despite 13pp oracle headroom). Diagnostic: instance degeneracy, LP compression, persistence under reduced degeneracy. Supervised verifier closes 8.3% gap.\n\n## Current Scores After Cross-Sharing\n\n| | Soundness | Excitement | Overall |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| R1 (Methods) | 3.0 | 3.0 (revised from 3.5) | 3.0 |\n| R2 (Novelty) | 3.0 (revised from 3.5) | 2.5 | 3.0 |\n\nBoth recommend **Findings** over Main.\n\n## Key Disagreements to Resolve\n\n### 1. Tautology vs Empirical Finding\n- R2 argues 4/5 signals trivially cannot select (they're per-instance aggregates), so the \"QE-selection decoupling\" is partially tautological. The only empirical content is LP (per-sample) also failing.\n- R1 initially rated this as \"genuinely novel\" but acknowledged R2's point partially, revising Excitement down.\n- R1 also noted that SJ may actually produce per-sample scores (mean pairwise similarity of sample_i against others), creating a definitional confusion in the paper.\n- **Resolution needed**: Is the decoupling a genuine contribution or a presentation artifact?\n\n### 2. Instance Degeneracy: Rebranding vs Novel Characterization\n- R2: Snell et al. 2024 already discusses compute-optimal allocation conditioning on difficulty. \"Instance degeneracy\" rebrands known model convergence.\n- R1: The paper provides concrete empirical thresholds and task-specific characterization that goes beyond abstract discussion. Not mere relabeling.\n- **Resolution needed**: Does the empirical characterization add value beyond naming?\n\n### 3. LoRA Rank Ablation: Strongest or Overrated?\n- Both agree it's the best-designed experiment.\n- R1: Elegant causal design showing multi-causality — genuine diagnostic value.\n- R2: Merely confirms what calibration literature predicts (fine-tuning sharpens distributions). Known from Kadavath et al. 2022.\n- **Resolution needed**: Is this experiment a contribution in the structured IE context, even if the phenomenon is known abstractly?\n\n### 4. Title Overclaiming\n- Both agree \"Cannot\" is too strong. \"Do Not\" or \"Fail To\" better matches evidence.\n- This is a minor point but affects how contribution is perceived.\n\n### 5. Missing Baselines\n- R1: Entity-token-only LP (the paper's own hypothesis about LP dilution) not tested — missed opportunity.\n- R2: Semantic entropy not evaluated — most theoretically motivated UQ signal.\n- R2: CoCoA comparison unfair — only linear combination tested, not MBR-style.\n- **Resolution needed**: Are these missing baselines fatal or addressable in revision?\n\n### 6. Numerical Inconsistencies\n- Both flagged AUROC 0.82 in abstract vs table values, rho claims, verifier gap closure numbers.\n- Appendix A self-audit catches some but not all.\n- **Resolution needed**: How much does this affect soundness score?\n\n## Your Task\n\nAs Area Chair, synthesize the convergence discussion:\n\n1. For each disagreement, state the resolved position (or acknowledge irreconcilable difference).\n2. Arrive at consensus scores or explain the range.\n3. Provide a final venue recommendation: Main / Findings / Reject.\n4. List the top 3 required revisions and top 3 suggestions.\n5. Write a meta-review paragraph (150-200 words) summarizing the assessment.\n\nBe specific and evidence-based. Reference the paper's actual numbers."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3103,"cache_read_input_tokens":66474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3103},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d14e849-04d8-4a95-8f72-941f894ab1f4","uuid":"46c72c40-fd3d-4b25-bddf-54223bbb0619"}
